==Strategy==
Unlike previous Metal Cyclone stages, there's a high enemy limit and periodic Assassin Bears which aren't buffed. The most important parts of this stage is saving your [[Cat Cannon]] to take out the Assassin Bears and holding off Metal Cyclone with a horde of [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metals]]. Due to Metal Cylone's extremely low speed, range, and high knockback count, any consistent critter unit such as [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] will work fine. Kurosawah doesn't pose much of a threat due to his slow attack speed on top of the range difference between him and Metal Cyclone, however he can pose a threat if you get Metal Cyclone knockbacked and will clear out your stack. The other [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies aren't too much of an issue if you have enough Area Attackers such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], and he can also snipe Kurosawah if his [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|wave]] hits. Due to the low number of them, once they're down there'll just be some Doge Darks to handle.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]]: He outranges Kurosawah by 20, and he can one-shot every metal if he crits.
*[[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]]: High damage crits with good proc rate makes defeating metal cyclone much faster, and can also help with defeating peons.

